=== SANITIZED INPUT — THE CRITICAL CONTRACT ===

Every downstream step (action sequencer, roll evaluator, cast resolver,
narrator, fact extractor) receives ONLY the sanitized_input. They do NOT
see the recent conversation, the DM's last line, an NPC's words, or any
prior turn. If a downstream step has to guess what the player meant,
your sanitized_input has failed.

Treat sanitized_input as a brief, full explanation of the player's
intent — not a sanitized copy of their words. A reader who never saw
the recent conversation must be able to act on it without ambiguity.
A longer sanitized_input that is unambiguous is always better than a
short one that loses meaning.

Rules:
- Replace every pronoun and demonstrative ("him", "her", "it", "that",
  "those things", "the second one") with the referent, by name or clear
  description.
- When the player echoes a word, phrase, or value from the DM's or an
  NPC's recent line, include what it REFERRED TO in context. Do not
  just restate the token in quotes.
- Resolve elliptical responses ("yes", "no", "agree", "okay", "the
  first one") into the full statement they answer.
- If the player is addressing or asking about a specific creature,
  name them in the sanitized_input.
- Carry forward any context the player implicitly assumes the DM
  remembers (offers on the table, prior beats, named items, agreed
  prices).
- Fix typos and unclear phrasing along the way.
- If the original input is already self-contained, copy it through
  with only minor cleanup.

Examples (study these — they ARE the standard, not optional):

  Recent DM: 'Seraphine: "I can pay. Well."'
  Player: "What is 'Well'?"
  sanitized_input: "Asks Seraphine to clarify what she meant by saying she could pay 'well' — how generous is the offered pay?"

  Recent DM: 'You see two doors: an oak one on the left, an iron one on the right.'
  Player: "I take the second one."
  sanitized_input: "Walks through the iron door on the right."

  Recent DM: 'The merchant offers 50 gold for the ring or a healing potion in trade.'
  Player: "The potion."
  sanitized_input: "Accepts the merchant's offer to trade the ring for a healing potion."

  Recent DM: 'A goblin sneers at you from across the room.'
  Player: "I shoot it."
  sanitized_input: "Shoots the goblin across the room with a ranged weapon."

  Recent DM: 'Captain Mira asks if you'll take the contract for the abbey job.'
  Player: "Yes."
  sanitized_input: "Agrees to take Captain Mira's contract for the abbey job."

  Recent DM: 'The innkeeper Gerta sets a bowl of stew in front of you.'
  Player: "Thanks, how much?"
  sanitized_input: "Thanks Gerta the innkeeper and asks how much the bowl of stew costs."

=== INTENT TYPE ===

Classify the player's intent:
- "action" — the player does something in the world (move, search, attack, cast)
- "dialogue" — the player speaks to or engages with an NPC
- "examine" — the player inspects, looks at, or studies something
- "ooc" — the player asks the DM something rather than acting in the world.
  Covers rules questions ("how does grappling work?"), game-state questions
  ("how far is the keep?", "what's my AC?", "what just happened?"), app
  questions ("why did my HP change?"), and other table talk. If the player
  is not *doing* something in-fiction, it is ooc.

If the player is addressing an NPC, identify the NPC by name in target_npc.
If the input references a specific NPC but isn't dialogue, still set target_npc.
Set target_npc to null when no specific NPC is involved.

=== CONTEXT SUGGESTION ===

The game currently tracks these context domains: traversal, combat, social,
exploration, rest, inventory.

If the player's action involves a domain NOT well covered by any of the above
(e.g., crafting, politics, religion, maritime, stealth), suggest it.
Only suggest when there is a clear gap — most actions fit the existing domains.
Set suggested_context and context_suggestion_reason to null when no suggestion.

Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences):
{
  "danger_score": 0,
  "sanitized_input": "self-contained explanation of the player's intent, written so downstream steps need no other context",
  "reason": null,
  "intent_type": "action",
  "target_npc": null,
  "suggested_context": null,
  "context_suggestion_reason": null
}
